@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@studentId = 1
@courseId = 1
@enrollmentId = 1

### 1. Crear curso y estudiante activo
# Ejecutar primero estas dos solicitudes y ajustar los ids si la base ya contiene datos.
POST {{baseUrl}}/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bases de Datos",
  "level": "intermediate"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Torres",
  "email": "ana.torres@example.com",
  "age": 21,
  "career": "Ingenieria de Software",
  "semester": 7,
  "isActive": true
}

### 2. Crear matrícula válida
POST {{baseUrl}}/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": {{studentId}},
  "courseId": {{courseId}}
}

### 3. Reiniciar la API y consultar la misma matrícula
GET {{baseUrl}}/enrollments?studentId={{studentId}}&courseId={{courseId}}

### 4. Matrícula duplicada (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": {{studentId}},
  "courseId": {{courseId}}
}

### 5. Matricular un estudiante inactivo (400)
# Cambiar el id al de un estudiante existente y desactivarlo antes de ejecutar.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/students/{{studentId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isActive": false
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": {{studentId}},
  "courseId": 2
}

### 6. Filtrar matrículas por estudiante o curso
GET {{baseUrl}}/enrollments?studentId={{studentId}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/enrollments?courseId={{courseId}}

### 7. Cancelar la matrícula y comprobar 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/enrollments/{{enrollmentId}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/enrollments/{{enrollmentId}}
# La solicitud anterior debe responder 404 después de la cancelación.
